      "side": 1,
      "message": "`fetchJSON()` enables server error reporting by default and then calls `fetch()`\n\n```\nreq.reportServerError ??\u003d true;\n```\n\nThen `loadPermissions()` handles the failed request and keeps the buttons hidden. By that point, the global error has already been reported.\n\nWe should probably override this behaviour by passing an error function callback that prevents the error from being propagated globally, something like:\n\n\n```\nreturn this._restApiHelper.fetchJSON({\n  url: `/changes/${changeNum}/permissions`,\n  anonymizedUrl: \u0027/changes/*/permissions\u0027,\n  // If the permission check fails, leave the AI review controls hidden.\n  errFn: () \u003d\u003e {},\n}) as Promise\u003cChangePermissionsInfo | undefined\u003e;\n```\n\nCan we add a test to check this behavior?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 333,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 333,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a20a35ae4a4192ae776e1c9724b64dddb5167846",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
